# TODO

## 0.3.1

1. DAG: de-duplicate predecessors, so that DAG.parse([[:a, :b], [:a, :b, :c]]) gives :b the predecessor :a once rather than twice.
2. DAG#cyclic_nodes in linear time: trimming forward from the nodes with no predecessors and back from those with no successors, leaving the nodes on a cycle, or on a path between two, as now.

## 0.4.0

3. Digraph: built from edges, and with add_node and add_edge; nodes and edges; predecessors and successors; attributes on nodes and edges.

## Digraph, after 0.4.0

4. each_node and each_edge.
5. In- and out-degree.
6. A filtered subgraph.

## DAG

7. A taken or running state, so that take(n) can hand out a batch to be run in parallel without handing it out again.
8. A hook for merging nodes of the same name, so that a subclass carrying more than a name need not override initialize and ready.
